.TH TECH2-CARDWRITER 1 "2026-10-25" "tech2-cardwriter 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tech2-cardwriter \- write Saab and GM Tech 2 PCMCIA card images from Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tech2-cardwriter
.\" options
.RB [ \-\-image
.IR IMAGE ]
.RB [ \-\-port
.IR DEVICE ]
.RB [ \-\-debug ]
.RB [ \-\-launch ]
.RB [ \-\-list-ports ]
.RB [ \-\-inspect
.IR IMAGE ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-h ]
.RI [ FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tech2-cardwriter
is a GTK4/libadwaita front-end for the freeware Windows program
.B Tech2 Card Writer
written by AlexRE in 2011.
It runs the original
.B Card_writer.exe
through a private Wine prefix, using a bundled Wine runtime in packaged builds
or the system Wine in a source install, so no Windows installation and no
TIS2000 installation are required.
.PP
The application scans the system for serial ports
.RB ( /dev/ttyUSB* ,
.BR /dev/ttyACM* ,
.BR /dev/ttyS* ),
validates a Tech 2
.B .bin
card image (the
.RB \(lq T2  \(rq
header and a size of exactly 10\ MB or 32\ MB), exposes the selected port as
.B COM1
inside the Wine prefix, and then opens Card Writer.
.PP
.B tech2-cardwriter
only writes the Tech 2 memory card.
It does not program ECUs, does not talk to the vehicle, and is not a
replacement for TIS2000 or SPS.
.PP
With no options it opens the graphical window.
A card image may be passed as an optional positional
.IR FILE
or with
.BR \-\-image .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-image " IMAGE"
Pre-select the card image
.I IMAGE
in the graphical window.
.TP
.BI \-\-port " DEVICE"
Pre-select the serial device
.I DEVICE
(for example
.IR /dev/ttyUSB0 )
instead of the first detected port.
.TP
.B \-\-launch
Start Card Writer immediately without opening the main window.
The port is taken from
.B \-\-port
or, if omitted, from the first detected serial port.
.TP
.B \-\-list-ports
List detected serial ports with their access status and exit.
Prints one line per port and returns a non-zero status if none are found.
.TP
.BI \-\-inspect " IMAGE"
Validate the card image
.I IMAGE
and print its size, version, header status, coverage and warnings, then exit.
Returns a non-zero status if the image is not a valid Tech 2 image.
.TP
.B \-\-debug
Keep Wine diagnostic output and set
.BR TECH2_DEBUG .
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print a short help message and exit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tech2-cardwriter/
Per-user data directory.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tech2-cardwriter/prefix/
The private Wine prefix, created on first launch.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tech2-cardwriter/images/
Optional library directory for card images.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/tech2-cardwriter/logs/
Log files.
.B wineboot.log
is written while the prefix is created and
.B cardwriter-YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS.log
captures the output of each Card Writer run.
.TP
.I ~/.cache/tech2-cardwriter/
Per-user cache directory.
.TP
.I /opt/tech2-cardwriter/
Installation root for a packaged build; contains
.BR app/Card_writer.exe ,
.BR lib/ ,
.BR share/ ,
and a bundled
.B wine/
runtime.
.TP
.I /usr/local/lib/tech2-cardwriter/
Default installation root for a source install
.RB ( "make install" ).
.TP
.I /usr/local/bin/tech2-cardwriter
Launcher for a source install.
.TP
.I /usr/bin/tech2-cardwriter
Launcher for the packaged build.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TECH2_CARDWRITER_ROOT
Overrides the installation root (the directory containing
.BR app/ ,
.BR lib/ ,
.BR share/ ,
and
.BR wine/ ).
.TP
.B TECH2_PORT
Adds an extra serial device to the detected port list, even if it does not
match the usual device patterns.
.TP
.B TECH2_DEBUG
Keep Wine debugging output when set to a non-empty value.
.TP
.B WINEPREFIX
Set internally to the private prefix before Wine is started; do not rely on
an external value.
.TP
.B XDG_DATA_HOME, XDG_STATE_HOME, XDG_CACHE_HOME
Override the per-user data, state and cache locations.
.TP
.B DISPLAY, WAYLAND_DISPLAY
The graphical session used to show the window and Card Writer.
.SH EXAMPLES
List the serial adapters that are currently plugged in:
.PP
.nf
.RS
tech2-cardwriter \-\-list-ports
.RE
.fi
.PP
Check a downloaded card image before writing it:
.PP
.nf
.RS
tech2-cardwriter \-\-inspect ~/Saab/saab_148.000.bin
.RE
.fi
.PP
Open the GUI with the usual port and image already selected:
.PP
.nf
.RS
tech2-cardwriter \-\-port /dev/ttyUSB0 \-\-image ~/Saab/saab_148.000.bin
.RE
.fi
.PP
Launch Card Writer directly and then choose COM1 and the image inside it:
.PP
.nf
.RS
tech2-cardwriter \-\-launch \-\-port /dev/ttyUSB0
.RE
.fi
.SH SAFETY
Use a stable 12\ V DC supply for the Tech 2.
A 32\ MB card write takes roughly 15 minutes; do not interrupt power, do not
unplug the serial cable and do not remove the PCMCIA card while Card Writer is
writing.
An interrupted write is not fatal, but the card must be written again before
it can be used.
.PP
Do not use CANdi on 2005 and older Saab vehicles; CANdi is only for 9-5 from
model year 2006 onward.
Card writing itself uses the Tech 2 RS-232 port and does not require CANdi.
.PP
Starting a write overwrites the whole PCMCIA card.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR wine (1),
.BR setserial (8)
.PP
